        "original_id": "3a74a585-db3f-5c11-b34f-e9ef9f81f88a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Fort Davis, Alaska\n- People: Jefferson C. Davis\n- Roles: military commander of Alaska, United States Army officer\n- Events: American Civil War\n\nFacts:\n- Jefferson C. Davis was born on March 2, 1828.\n- Jefferson C. Davis was a regular officer of the United States Army during the American Civil War.\n- In 1862, Jefferson C. Davis killed a superior officer.\n- Jefferson C. Davis served as the military commander of Alaska from 1868 to 1870.\n- Fort Davis, Alaska, was named for General Jefferson C. Davis.\n- Jefferson C. Davis was known for the similarity of his name to Confederate President Jefferson Davis.\n- Jefferson C. Davis died on November 30, 1879.",
